"- Land checklist: resolve review findings or record them as known bugs in their feature's file; use `nana-land` with a clean `main` checkout and clean source, verified review rounds, and CI or the local suite on the reviewed tip; where the project's `AGENTS.md` says CI covers its suite, on the fast-forward path, `nana-land` runs the suite only when the tip's CI cannot stand in; the clean-merge path refuses instead. Revalidate if either checkout changes, and rely on the helper's immediate pre-merge checks, ff-only merge, and containment verification. Where origin is on github.com and the tip tracks a workflow, `nana-land` also refuses until the newest CI run of each workflow for the tip has passed, so push the tip to its open pull request, do not cancel its run, and wait for CI. When main has moved since the accepted tip, `nana-land` merges current main into it; a merge with no conflict lands without new CI or review, and a conflict only in the generated files the land contract names, rebuilt by their own generators, counts as no conflict; every other conflicting merge refuses, so merge main in the lane and get that tip reviewed and through CI. In nana-pi, lanes land without waiting for Windows; Windows runs on main after each land, and a red main blocks further lands. Linux remains advisory. Every commit reaching main must be covered by a revision every reviewer accepted; the one exemption is that conflict-free merge, including generated-file conflicts resolved by their own generators; there are no others, and never commit directly to main. Put HANDOFF and session notes in the reviewed change before its final round; nothing is written after a land. Cleanup is a separate operation, only for a clean `feat/<lane>` worktree contained in `main`. Then run map and README checks and the suite check this project's AGENTS.md names; commit explicit paths and report evidence.": 0 matches
