"Run `node packages/nana-setup/bin/install-check.mjs` from the repository root. The check installs nana into a temporary home, registers the checked-out pi extensions, installs pi-subagents, starts a pi RPC session, runs one scripted pi turn, runs one offline review through each installed pi-review launcher against a throwaway repository, simulates Claude Code hook dispatch, and runs doctor. After doctor it starts one offline lane build through each installed pi-worker launcher, in its own linked worktree of that throwaway repository. The scripted turn, reviews and builds use local test models: they make no network request and call no real model. Before the builds, the check points the temporary home's roster builder at the test model and lists the review fixture in pi's user settings. Its child processes receive the temporary home and temporary/cache folders; the sanitized base environment removes `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, `PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, nana's override variables and caller npm configuration. Each build adds only `PI_OFFLINE=1`. The check does not install nana into the caller's real home. The check depends on Node, Git, pi and npm registry access. The pi-subagents install is retried up to three times, five seconds apart, after an exit failure, and each failed attempt prints a NOTE line with npm's error-code line.": 0 matches
