"The reviewer adds `--setting-sources project,local`, an external `--settings` file and `--strict-mcp-config` after its tool lists. The settings file sets `claudeMdExcludes` to absolute ancestor paths for CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE.local.md, .claude/CLAUDE.md and .claude/rules/**, from the reviewed tree's parent through the filesystem root. The cwd stays the reviewed tree; its own `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` and rules remain eligible. This requires Claude Code's supported `claudeMdExcludes` setting (confirmed in 2.1.310); managed/policy instructions cannot be excluded. `project,local` alone is insufficient: Claude can label home rules as ancestor Project memory. It no longer inherits user rules, user CLAUDE.md, user hooks, user MCP instructions or auto-memory. In particular it loses the rulings, objective, verifier-pipe hook and user `permissions.defaultMode`; tools outside its allowlist are denied in print mode. Its inputs are the brief, feature known bugs and review standard, plus project/local context. Its settings seal `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1`, `NANA_ROLE=reviewer` and `NANA_HANDOFF=off`. `--effort` comes from the exact roster model key in user `modelSettings`, else top-level `effortLevel`, else no flag; aliases are not expanded. The shared carry helper prints a value-free `claude-review:` diagnostic. Normal exit, recording failure and handled SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP remove the settings folder. Windows also starts the existing detached cleanup watcher, without a build record or lane lock, because its SIGTERM forcibly stops the process. A POSIX hard kill, or a kill before the Windows watcher starts, can leave the folder.": 0 matches
