cated GitHub CLI, like the land tool; its tests inject Node fake gh commands. A successful land prints one `ci:` line per workflow; elsewhere one land note says why CI was not read. After a CI-checked merge, it reads the tip\'s CI suite records, keeps them in the clone\'s ci-runs store, and prints the reader\'s lines. It notes each non-skipped file at or above half its record\'s per-file limit. The records read stops after its total budget; a read or store failure becomes one land note and never refuses the completed land. The helper retries a nonzero run-list exit once, never a timeout or spawn error. Passing CI stands in for the local suite only when every highest-attempt same-platform leg record from a judged run has an empty `filters` array, final files and exit 0. On the fast-forward path, missing or old records and failed or over-budget reads require the local suite. A lane changing a workflow or the canonical test runner also requires it, even with passing CI. The helper prints one `suite:` line naming CI\'s run, attempt and platform, or local with its reason. End records carry `suite` and `suiteWhy`; CI lands have null `suiteMs`, and record readers show `suite ci`. Otherwise the helper runs the suite in the source tree with `NANA_LAND_TIP` set to the source tip\'s full SHA. Off Windows, the locked suite measures the runtime map; on Windows, it runs once without measuring and prints a land note. After a passing local suite it also writes the product report for the tip and prints a land note naming the page. CI lands refresh neither the runtime map, the land report nor local suite records; hand runs and fallback lands refresh them. Lines the suite prints with the `[nana-land]` land-note prefix appear in success output too. Immediately before merging it rechecks both checkouts, the verdicts, live reservations and main\'s captured HEAD under the ledger lock. Kept review text is not a land prerequisite and produces no land notes. It performs one `git merge --ff-only`, verifies containment, and requires the main ref equal to the tip or its merge commit with clean tracked state before success. Do not operate the main checkout during a land: a branch switch in the instant between the final check and merge is not defended, but a detected switch prevents success and the helper refuses afterwards without success records. Git refuses an untracked collision with a landed path. The helper never pushes or writes HANDOFF/session archive text. A legacy version-1 LAND does not authorize a land; every pre-change revision needs a fresh review. On success the helper prints the push command and release status. An attempt that reaches land recording writes a start and, when ended, an end record; an interrupted attempt may leave only its start, while argument refusals and a `--main` outside any repository write nothing, and each ended attempt ends with one `[nana-land] land record:` line. After a successful merge it prints the shared local `releaseStatus` result, which exports `selectReleaseTag` and `countTemplateCommits`, reports main against origin/main as of the last fetch, never fetches, and never runs `git tag` because its named form creates a tag.': 0 matches
