"at ~8 ms on the real index, inside a ~60 ms Node start. A query may wait up to 100 ms on a database lock, and a build up to 5 s. After an open or query failure, the hook closes its handle and pauses 50 ms before retrying, up to 10 total attempts. Each attempt reserves the query's 100 ms busy timeout plus 150 ms for the rest of the pull; a pause runs only when that reserve still fits. Its log records numeric `attempts`, the first failure in `retried` and the latest subsequent failure in `failure`, using structured error codes rather than private error messages. A `setTimeout(process.exit(0))": 0 matches
